{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 14223 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "9c669abaace525a19f3cc2af6b27913898e36e49aeb69a72ca2af73dfb3b9f8a" :edb/db-before-t 14222 :edb/db-after-t 14223 :edb/tx-data [[13194139547535 50 #inst "2026-11-11T22:35:46.724Z" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186045416 1117 #edb/ref 17592186760628 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186045416 1118 #edb/ref 17592186048326 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186045416 1118 #edb/ref 17592186049371 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186045416 1118 #edb/ref 17592186049719 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186045416 1118 #edb/ref 17592186049891 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186045416 1118 #edb/ref 17592186050252 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186045416 1118 #edb/ref 17592186050633 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760616 1080 "\\begin{pmatrix}2&-4\\\\10&8\\end{pmatrix}" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760616 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760616 1083 #uuid "00a14bb6-f631-5f70-8977-1482a5f75eac" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760617 1080 "Let $\\mathbf x\\in\\mathbb R^n$ be arbitrary. Since the $\\mathbf v_i$ form a basis, there are scalars $c_1,\\ldots,c_n$ with $\\mathbf x=\\sum_{i=1}^n c_i\\mathbf v_i$. By linearity and the assumed equality on basis vectors,\n$$S(\\mathbf x)=S\\!\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^n c_i\\mathbf v_i\\right)=\\sum_{i=1}^n c_iS(\\mathbf v_i)=\\sum_{i=1}^n c_iT(\\mathbf v_i)=T\\!\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^n c_i\\mathbf v_i\\right)=T(\\mathbf x).$$\nThus $S$ and $T$ agree on every vector in their common domain, so $S=T$. Spanning supplies the expansion; the proof does not require computing its coefficients." 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760617 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760617 1083 #uuid "01775553-2e48-5875-9150-22cb6950bb30" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760618 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049719 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760618 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049891 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760618 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050407 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760618 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050633 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760618 1089 #edb/ref 17592186760680 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760618 1090 #uuid "0587c431-ef44-575a-8698-e64c3d56f4c7" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760619 1068 #edb/ref 17592186760622 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760619 1068 #edb/ref 17592186760646 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760619 1071 "Source question: Assignment item (2); Kuttler 2017A, Exercise 5.2.4, printed p. 278 (PDF p. 290). The handout recommends Procedure 5.10 and Example 5.11.\n\nSuppose $T$ is a linear transformation such that\n$$T\\!\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\1\\\\-8\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\3\\\\1\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad\nT\\!\\begin{pmatrix}-1\\\\0\\\\6\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}2\\\\4\\\\1\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad\nT\\!\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\-1\\\\3\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}6\\\\1\\\\-1\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nFind the matrix $A$ of $T$, that is, $T(\\mathbf x)=A\\mathbf x$. Show supporting work.\n\n$A=$ {{matrix}}." 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760619 1072 #uuid "0ad61779-481f-5a72-a1fc-d5ace5fa7378" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760619 1074 "The given inputs are not the standard basis: their images are the columns of $AP$, not directly the columns of $A$. Solve $AP=Q$ by right-multiplying by $P^{-1}$, or solve the three corresponding systems for the rows of $A$." 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760620 1075 #edb/ref 17592186760638 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760620 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760620 1077 "response" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760620 1078 #edb/ref 17592186760638 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760620 1079 #uuid "0c278b5b-4ec2-5e77-89be-a83c2a7b3a5e" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760621 1058 #edb/ref 17592186760665 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760621 1062 #uuid "1dd26e72-3dff-56ab-b7b2-c585da3a7aaf" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760621 1063 #edb/ref 17592186760670 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760622 1075 #edb/ref 17592186760679 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760622 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760622 1077 "response" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760622 1078 #edb/ref 17592186760679 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760622 1079 #uuid "210bdfeb-e6e5-5c23-86d5-d7ccc9190c3e" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760623 1058 #edb/ref 17592186760656 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760623 1062 #uuid "2b614e54-daad-580b-8de0-580526158e32" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760623 1063 #edb/ref 17592186760652 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760624 1080 "7" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760624 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760624 1083 #uuid "2ea5e46e-b655-5c23-9009-3b88eddb24ca" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760625 1080 "The composition applies $T$ first, then $S$, so $(S\\circ T)(\\mathbf x)=B(A\\mathbf x)=(BA)\\mathbf x$. Thus\n$$BA=\\begin{pmatrix}0&-2\\\\4&2\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}3&1\\\\-1&2\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}2&-4\\\\10&8\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nThen\n$$\\begin{pmatrix}2&-4\\\\10&8\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}2\\\\-1\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}8\\\\12\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nIndependently, $T(2,-1)^T=(5,-4)^T$, and $S(5,-4)^T=(8,12)^T$, confirming the order and result." 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760625 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760625 1083 #uuid "37f6e35e-1720-59c1-a040-01cc1f370f66" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760626 1080 "Using the standard positive (counterclockwise) rotation convention,\n$$R=\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos(2\\pi/3)&-\\sin(2\\pi/3)\\\\\\sin(2\\pi/3)&\\cos(2\\pi/3)\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-\\frac12&-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}&-\\frac12\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nReflection across the $x$ axis has matrix $F=\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\0&-1\\end{pmatrix}$. Since rotation occurs first, the required matrix is\n$$FR=\\begin{pmatrix}-\\frac12&-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}&\\frac12\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nFor a check, $e_1$ rotates to $(-1/2,\\sqrt3/2)^T$, then reflects to $(-1/2,-\\sqrt3/2)^T$, the first column. The second column follows from $e_2$ in the same way." 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760626 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760626 1083 #uuid "386c50c3-709b-5213-a1b5-ccc8d909870a" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760627 1075 #edb/ref 17592186760633 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760627 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760627 1077 "matrix" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760627 1078 #edb/ref 17592186760633 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760627 1079 #uuid "3987f90d-443a-5c35-9112-6c4b7640d536" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760628 1043 #edb/ref 17592186760621 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760628 1043 #edb/ref 17592186760623 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760628 1043 #edb/ref 17592186760645 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760628 1043 #edb/ref 17592186760647 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760628 1043 #edb/ref 17592186760648 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760628 1043 #edb/ref 17592186760656 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760628 1043 #edb/ref 17592186760665 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760628 1043 #edb/ref 17592186760673 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760628 1043 #edb/ref 17592186760678 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760628 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045461 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760628 1045 "MTH 341 — WHW-6" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760628 1046 #edb/ref 17592186760621 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760628 1047 #inst "2026-11-12T07:59:00.000Z" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760628 1048 #edb/ref 17592186405206 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760628 1053 #uuid "3ec70bdc-5ecf-5d25-ba19-e5e6f998ae86" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760629 1068 #edb/ref 17592186760644 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760629 1068 #edb/ref 17592186760653 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760629 1071 "Source question: Assignment item (1), handout p. 1.\n\nSuppose $A$ is a $7\\times9$ matrix with $\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=2$. What is the dimension of the row space of $A$? Briefly justify your answer. Remember that an example is just an example; it does not cover every possibility.\n\n$\\dim\\operatorname{Row}(A)=$ {{dimension}}. Give the justification in the written response." 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760629 1072 #uuid "42347e15-642d-5b7d-9335-656a5b86cb76" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760629 1074 "Use the nine columns for rank-nullity. The resulting rank is also the dimension of the row space; the seven rows give a consistent upper bound, not the initial rank-nullity total." 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760630 1084 #edb/ref 17592186760634 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760630 1084 #edb/ref 17592186760641 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760630 1085 "Source question: Assignment item (3); Kuttler 2017A, Exercise 5.2.8(a)–(b), printed p. 279 (PDF p. 291). The handout cites p. 280; the assigned parts are on the preceding page.\n\nFor each assigned function $T:\\mathbb R^3\\to\\mathbb R^2$, show that it is a linear transformation and determine its matrix. Only parts (a) and (b) are assigned." 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760630 1086 #uuid "461fea4b-21e5-5078-a2fa-9de631fdc944" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760630 1087 #edb/ref 17592186760641 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760631 1068 #edb/ref 17592186760620 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760631 1071 "Source question: Assignment item (4); Kuttler 2017A, Exercise 5.2.9(a) only, printed p. 280 (PDF p. 292).\n\nConsider $T:\\mathbb R^3\\to\\mathbb R^2$ defined by\n$$T\\!\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\\\z\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}x+2y+3z+1\\\\2y-3x+z\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nExplain why $T$ is not linear." 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760631 1072 #uuid "46bf94b4-458b-5c3e-804b-042b8a4fd877" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760631 1074 "Test a necessary linearity property. The constant $+1$ makes the zero input produce a nonzero output. A counterexample disproves linearity; checking a few successful inputs would not prove it." 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760632 1080 "Reading coefficients in the order $x,y,z$ gives\n$$A=\\begin{pmatrix}7&2&1\\\\3&-11&2\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad T(\\mathbf x)=A\\mathbf x.$$\nFor all $\\mathbf u,\\mathbf v\\in\\mathbb R^3$ and scalars $\\alpha,\\beta$,\n$$T(\\alpha\\mathbf u+\\beta\\mathbf v)=A(\\alpha\\mathbf u+\\beta\\mathbf v)=\\alpha A\\mathbf u+\\beta A\\mathbf v=\\alpha T(\\mathbf u)+\\beta T(\\mathbf v).$$\nTherefore $T$ is linear." 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760632 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760632 1083 #uuid "4ba2450b-9191-5719-9d3a-3e62924942b9" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760633 1080 "\\begin{pmatrix}-\\frac12&-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}&\\frac12\\end{pmatrix}" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760633 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760633 1083 #uuid "4dc8418e-05c6-5356-ba24-b3cd64c48f43" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760634 1062 #uuid "4ea7d960-e404-5ad9-8e20-0fb387160200" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760634 1063 #edb/ref 17592186760662 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760635 1080 "The rank-nullity theorem uses the number of columns, so $\\operatorname{rank}(A)+\\operatorname{nullity}(A)=9$. Thus $\\operatorname{rank}(A)=9-2=7$. Row rank equals column rank, so $\\dim\\operatorname{Row}(A)=7$. This applies to every matrix satisfying the hypotheses." 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760635 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760635 1083 #uuid "4fbfa299-1597-55c0-894e-66d5e503e601" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760636 1068 #edb/ref 17592186760663 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760636 1068 #edb/ref 17592186760664 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760636 1071 "**(a)** $T\\!\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\\\z\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}x+2y+3z\\\\2y-3x+z\\end{pmatrix}$.\n\nShow that $T$ is linear and determine $A$ such that $T(\\mathbf x)=A\\mathbf x$.\n\n$A=$ {{matrix}}. Give the linearity justification in the written response." 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760636 1072 #uuid "5402f38e-9495-519d-8e62-16c3b411d8bd" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760636 1074 "Reorder the second component as $-3x+2y+z$ before reading its coefficients. A $2\\times3$ matrix has three input components and two output components; distributivity proves linearity." 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760637 1075 #edb/ref 17592186760617 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760637 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760637 1077 "response" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760637 1078 #edb/ref 17592186760617 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760637 1079 #uuid "54b9db46-6b90-5678-9e8e-0d44dac9d729" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760638 1080 "Every linear map sends the zero vector to the zero vector, because $T(\\mathbf0)=T(0\\mathbf v)=0T(\\mathbf v)=\\mathbf0$. Here\n$$T\\!\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\0\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}\\ne\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nTherefore this $T$ is not linear. This single counterexample disproves a property that a linear map must satisfy for every input." 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760638 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760638 1083 #uuid "58af6c35-6ff6-5ad6-81e4-0aeb5432df34" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760639 1080 "\\begin{pmatrix}8\\\\12\\end{pmatrix}" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760639 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760639 1083 #uuid "5d9296e0-9bdc-5270-8318-b7b6ced8d948" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760640 1080 "\\begin{pmatrix}52&21&9\\\\44&23&8\\\\5&4&1\\end{pmatrix}" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760640 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760640 1083 #uuid "5f717238-c4d2-56f6-b4aa-afa0f297acd7" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760641 1058 #edb/ref 17592186760634 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760641 1062 #uuid "627e00ee-d490-542c-9d37-c9a69f590296" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760641 1063 #edb/ref 17592186760636 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760642 1080 "\\begin{pmatrix}-2&1\\\\5&-2\\end{pmatrix}" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760642 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760642 1083 #uuid "637c08ca-4ee8-5bfb-b4a1-5739d0056742" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760643 1080 "In the variable order $x,y,z$, the coefficient rows are $(1,2,3)$ and $(-3,2,1)$. Thus\n$$T(\\mathbf x)=A\\mathbf x,\\qquad A=\\begin{pmatrix}1&2&3\\\\-3&2&1\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nFor arbitrary $\\mathbf u,\\mathbf v\\in\\mathbb R^3$ and $\\alpha,\\beta\\in\\mathbb R$,\n$$T(\\alpha\\mathbf u+\\beta\\mathbf v)=A(\\alpha\\mathbf u+\\beta\\mathbf v)=\\alpha A\\mathbf u+\\beta A\\mathbf v=\\alpha T(\\mathbf u)+\\beta T(\\mathbf v).$$\nThis proves linearity, including both additivity and homogeneity." 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760643 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760643 1083 #uuid "63c34434-9673-51e5-9301-9cd70d084fdc" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760644 1075 #edb/ref 17592186760624 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760644 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760644 1077 "dimension" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760644 1078 #edb/ref 17592186760624 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760644 1079 #uuid "67392bb2-fa70-5825-8b29-9187721102a7" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760645 1058 #edb/ref 17592186760673 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760645 1062 #uuid "6ee551f8-4184-5884-b4aa-9c9ef6e51289" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760645 1063 #edb/ref 17592186760650 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760646 1075 #edb/ref 17592186760640 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760646 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760646 1077 "matrix" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760646 1078 #edb/ref 17592186760640 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760646 1079 #uuid "6eefb71d-cda8-56ee-98d2-bb30a6a8fac8" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760647 1062 #uuid "78c3392d-76f9-572d-9758-536009da4686" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760647 1063 #edb/ref 17592186760668 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760648 1058 #edb/ref 17592186760645 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760648 1062 #uuid "7ba7ea90-1082-5262-968e-4237126f994c" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760648 1063 #edb/ref 17592186760660 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760649 1068 #edb/ref 17592186760637 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760649 1071 "Source question: Assignment item (8), handout p. 1.\n\nLet $S$ and $T$ be linear transformations from $\\mathbb R^n$ to $\\mathbb R^n$, and let $\\{\\mathbf v_1,\\ldots,\\mathbf v_n\\}$ be a basis for $\\mathbb R^n$. Suppose $S(\\mathbf v_i)=T(\\mathbf v_i)$ for all $i=1,\\ldots,n$. Show that $S=T$. (This says that a linear transformation is determined by a basis!)" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760649 1072 #uuid "7e4d787a-bb35-555f-bf55-a770c964bfd1" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760649 1074 "Start with an arbitrary vector and expand it in the given basis. Apply linearity to both maps and use the hypothesis term by term. Agreement on the basis must be extended to every input before concluding that the functions are equal." 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760650 1088 #edb/ref 17592186048459 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760650 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050252 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760650 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050825 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760650 1089 #edb/ref 17592186760630 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760650 1090 #uuid "86a8c940-afbe-559e-b4f5-2034b26b3119" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760651 1075 #edb/ref 17592186760639 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760651 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760651 1077 "image" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760651 1078 #edb/ref 17592186760639 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760651 1079 #uuid "8778d74d-fe75-58f6-a455-ae03ba73364f" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760652 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049371 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760652 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049548 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760652 1089 #edb/ref 17592186760657 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760