\mathbf x)$ and then $S(T(\\mathbf x))$ separately." 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760656 1058 #edb/ref 17592186760647 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760656 1062 #uuid "a2253b6d-0514-5e8d-98dc-37848e96b4aa" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760656 1063 #edb/ref 17592186760618 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760657 1068 #edb/ref 17592186760654 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760657 1068 #edb/ref 17592186760661 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760657 1071 "Source question: Assignment item (6); Kuttler 2017A, Exercise 5.3.5, printed p. 286 (PDF p. 298).\n\nLet $T$ be the linear transformation induced by\n$$A=\\begin{pmatrix}2&1\\\\5&2\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nFind the matrix of $T^{-1}$. Show supporting work.\n\nMatrix of $T^{-1}$: {{matrix}}." 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760657 1072 #uuid "ab610f7b-2f7f-5059-a1d6-09cd6f38b97a" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760657 1074 "The matrix of the inverse transformation is the inverse matrix. Check the determinant before using the $2\\times2$ inverse formula, and distribute its negative reciprocal to every entry." 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760658 1088 #edb/ref 17592186048978 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760658 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049881 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760658 1089 #edb/ref 17592186760629 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760658 1090 #uuid "b1ce0d65-8223-5402-8d69-60bbbd03c390" 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760659 1080 "The determinant is $\\det A=2\\cdot2-1\\cdot5=-1\\ne0$, so the inverse transformation exists. It is induced by\n$$A^{-1}=\\frac1{-1}\\begin{pmatrix}2&-1\\\\-5&2\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-2&1\\\\5&-2\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nMultiplying in either order gives $AA^{-1}=A^{-1}A=I_2$, so $\\mathbf x\\mapsto A^{-1}\\mathbf x$ reverses $T$." 13194139547535 17592186502323 true] [17592186760659 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 1319413954